-- title:
--   No r-new parabolic eigenclass at level Mr
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, let $p$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, i.e. a two-dimensional space $V$ with a multiplicative action $\rho$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ factoring through a finite level, assumed absolutely irreducible (irreducible after base change to the algebraic closure of the residue field). Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$, let $M\neq 0$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, and let $r$ be a prime with $r\notin S$ and $r\nmid M$ such that for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $r$ a nonunit of $P$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $r$ for $P$ one has $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$. Assume the weight-two cusp forms of level $M$ admit an integral structure, and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathrm{heckeAlgebra}\,M\,2\,S$ (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$) to the residue field such that for every prime $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S$, and every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $\ell$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2-\theta(T_\ell)X+\ell$. Put $L=Mr$, with the two level comparisons $\mathrm{LevelLE}\,M\,L\,\top\,\top\,1$ and $\mathrm{LevelLE}\,M\,L\,\top\,\top\,r$ ($M\mid L$ and $1$, resp. $r$, dividing $L/M$, together with the unit condition). Let $F$ be a characteristic-zero field that is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with injective structure map, and let $c$ be an additive homomorphism from $\mathrm{Additive}\,\Gamma_0(L)$, presented as $\mathrm{GammaH}\,L\,\top$, to $F$ which is parabolic, i.e. lies in $\mathrm{parabolicHoms}$. Assume $c$ is a common eigenvector of the transfer-defined Hecke operators: for every prime $\ell\nmid L$ with $\ell\notin S$ one has $\mathrm{heckeT}\,L\,\top\,\ell\,F\,c=a_\ell\cdot c$ with $a_\ell\in F$; assume further that each such $a_\ell$ (with also $\ell\nmid M$) is a root of the image in $F[X]$ of some monic $P\in\mathcal{O}[X]$ for which there is $c_0\in\mathcal{O}$ with residue $\theta(T_\ell)$ and $P$ reducing modulo the maximal ideal to $(X-\overline{c_0})^{\deg P}$. Finally assume that both degeneracy maps $\mathrm{jDeg}$ from $H^1$ at level $L$ to $H^1$ at level $M$, the one with parameter $1$ and the one with parameter $r$, annihilate $c$. Then $c=0$.
--
--   This is the cohomological form of the absence of $r$-new congruences: when $\bar\rho$ admits no level-raising congruence at $r$, the $r$-new part of the parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_0(Mr)$ contains no eigenclass whose Hecke eigenvalues reduce to the residual system $\theta$. It is used in the corresponding statement about the $\sigma$-corner classes at the auxiliary level, which feeds the level-raising and lowering arguments via Ihara's lemma.
